# .dev.vars TEMPLATE — DO NOT put real secrets here.
#
# 1. Copy this file:    cp .dev.vars.template .dev.vars
# 2. Fill in real values in .dev.vars (NEVER commit it).
# 3. .dev.vars is in .gitignore — verify with `git check-ignore -v .dev.vars`.
# 4. For production, push secrets via wrangler:
#       wrangler secret put DATABASE_URL
#       wrangler secret put OPENAI_API_KEY
#       wrangler secret put STRIPE_SECRET_KEY
#       wrangler secret put JWT_SECRET
#    Wrangler stores them encrypted; they NEVER appear in wrangler.toml.
#
# WARNING: a single committed real secret is a breach. If you accidentally
# commit a value, rotate it (revoke + re-issue) BEFORE removing it from git
# history. Removing from history alone does not unrevoke a leaked secret.
# Tools that scan public repos (TruffleHog, GitGuardian, GitHub secret scanning)
# detect leaks within minutes — assume any pushed secret is compromised.

# DATABASE_URL=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# JWT_SECRET=
